UPDATE "gaps" SET "description" = 'READ VREDENBURGH ET AL. 2009 (REF-01002) IN FULL. IT IS THE FIRST ANCHORING-TIER STATED MAXIMUM THIS PARAMETER HAS HAD, AND IT IS HELD AT SKIM GRADE. The TRID/TRB record and its verbatim abstract were retrieved and persisted this batch (HTTP 200, 50825 bytes) and give: Results suggest that for a transit distance of up to 20 feet, a ramp should not exceed a maximum cross slope of 5% or a maximum running slope of 7%. THE ARTICLE ITSELF WAS NOT RETRIEVED. Journal of Architectural and Planning Research 26(2):145-158, ISSN 0738-0895, NO DOI -- which is why six batches of DOI-keyed searching never met it and why it sat unread inside REF-00977 reference list. WHAT THE FULL READ MUST SETTLE, none of which the abstract answers: (1) the participant count and composition -- the record says users of manual AND motorised wheelchairs and states no n, so the population match is graded PARTIAL on an unknown denominator; (2) the slope set actually tested, since 7% may be a recommendation or merely the highest slope at which perceived effort did not degrade, and those are different claims; (3) whether the 20-foot transit distance is a tested bound or an assumption; (4) whether disabled people shaped the study beyond serving as subjects, which under D-0178 is the difference between T1 and Co-1. ON RESOLUTION: promote extraction 45 from skim/preliminary, resolve determination gate 1, and re-determine parameter 3 x MOB -- or record that the abstract overstated. UNTIL THEN THE FIGURE DOES NOT MOVE. Specification 8 stands at 5% and is SAFE rather than correct: 7% is LOOSER, the parameter direction is lower_is_better, so the standing value errs conservative while its tier_basis (T4-6-only-threshold, rests_on_proxy_inference=1) describes the wrong evidence. Batch 15 refused to claim Co-1 for REF-01001 on an ambiguous abstract and the full text vindicated the refusal; this is the same discipline one column along. TRID also lists the publisher as Elsevier Science, which is wrong for this journal -- do not propagate it; the publisher field was left unwritten for that reason. || CORRECTED 2026-09-25: NOT-ADDRESSABLE, AND NOT QUEUED FOR ANYONE (batch 20). Owner ruling 2026-09-25, applied literally: ''if we can''t access something from anywhere then we have to give up on it for now.'' The full text this gap asks to be read is unreachable from anywhere this project can go (GAP-026, closed this batch as decided). The gap stays OPEN because its subject stays true -- the first anchoring-tier stated maximum on parameter 3 is held at skim grade on an abstract -- and closing it would read as though that had been fixed. It is marked NOT-ADDRESSABLE so that no sweep, runbook or session picks it up as work. Extraction 45 stays skim/preliminary, gate 1 stays unresolved, C10 keeps refusing. If a route that has never been tried presents itself without a search, it may be taken; nobody is to go looking. Side note, recorded here because this gap names the metadata question: the publisher''s table of contents (persisted this batch, 07da0016d338f0f8.pdf) gives the fourth author as ''Jerome M. Welner'', against the stored ''Weiner''; GAP-044 records why the row cannot be corrected.', "updated_at" = '2026-09-25 05:02', "updated_by_session" = 'session_2026-09-25-research-batch-20-audit-cluster-templer-fhwa', "mining_addressability" = 'NOT-ADDRESSABLE' WHERE "gap_id" = 'GAP-016';
UPDATE "gaps" SET "description" = 'THE CORPUS NOW HAS ZERO LIVE DETERMINATIONS, AND K01/K02 PASS BY HAVING NOTHING TO EXAMINE. Batch 16 retired specification 8 in place because K02 (blocking) requires a LIVE determination to account for every extraction of its parameter and this batch added five it did not hold; the engine could not recompute the cell (GAP-019). test_db_integrity then went 74/74 -- and K01 and K02 appear in its own PASSED HAVING EXAMINED NOTHING list, which grew from 19 to 22. THAT IS CLAUDE.md SECTION 5(a) VERBATIM, the failure mode this repository has produced four separate times: a gate that passes having examined nothing. IT IS RECORDED HERE RATHER THAN BANKED AS A GREEN RUN. The retirement is defensible -- a live cell omitting new evidence attests a subset while reading as the whole, which is K02 own stated reason, and the alternative was writing 7% onto a skim extraction from an abstract in a third-party index. But three things follow that a reader must not have to derive. (1) Nothing in the book now states a ramp gradient; specification 8 remains readable as history at 5% / 1:20 and is NOT live. (2) The green integrity run says less than it did yesterday, and comparing 74/74 today against 74/74 before this batch would be a false equivalence -- the denominator of examined checks fell. (3) This is the SECOND time in three batches that the determination surface emptied: batch 15 code review caught spec 7 retired and never re-determined, and fixed it by determining spec 8. It cannot be fixed the same way here, because the engine refuses. CLOSING CONDITION: GAP-016 full read, then GAP-019 engine ruling, then re-determine. Until both, parameter 3 x MOB is undetermined and determination gate 1 stays open. || CORRECTED 2026-09-25: BATCH 20: THE EMPTY DETERMINATION SURFACE IS AN ACCEPTED LIMITATION, NOT A QUEUED TASK. Owner ruling 2026-09-25, applied literally: ''if we can''t access something from anywhere then we have to give up on it for now.'' This