UPDATE "gaps" SET "description" = 'GAP-020 IS NOT CLOSED BY THE GAP-019 FIX, AND THE REASON IS NOW MECHANICAL RATHER THAN A JUDGEMENT CALL. With the engine repaired, re-determining parameter 3 x MOB was REHEARSED on a throwaway copy and it succeeds: state=provisional, value_max 7.0 percent, unit percent, tier_basis T1, governing_refs [REF-01002], rests_on_proxy_inference 0, with the cap recorded in the confidence flag naming gate 1. K01 and K02 return to 1 subject each, so two of the three vacuous checks GAP-020 records would be answered. BUT C10 THEN FAILS: no published cell rests on an unverified or disputed source -- 1 examined, 1 unsound -- because REF-01002 is UNVERIFIED, the grade batch 16 gave it after I4 caught the original VERIFIED as wrong (the article was never retrieved, only its TRID record). test_db_integrity goes 73/74 on the rehearsal. SO THE REPOSITORY OWN BLOCKING CHECK REFUSES THE RE-DETERMINATION, and it refuses it for exactly the reason batch 16 refused it by hand. That is the strongest possible form of the earlier caution: it is no longer my judgement that the cell should not be determined on an unread abstract, it is C10. THE EMPTY DETERMINATION SURFACE IS THEREFORE CORRECT UNTIL GAP-016 CLOSES, and the path out is now fully specified: read REF-01002 full text, verify it, re-determine, C10 passes, resolve gate 1. Nothing else is owed and nothing should be forced. DO NOT apply the rehearsed determination: it is in a scratch copy only, canonical is untouched, and applying it would turn a blocking gate red to fill a surface that is honestly empty. || CORRECTED 2026-09-25: BATCH 20: ACCEPTED LIMITATION, NOT A QUEUED TASK. Owner ruling 2026-09-25, applied literally: ''if we can''t access something from anywhere then we have to give up on it for now.'' This gap''s ''path out'' began ''read REF-01002 full text, verify it'' -- that step is given up on, so the path is closed rather than pending, and nothing is scheduled against it. Its instruction stands and is reinforced: DO NOT apply the rehearsed 7 percent determination. C10 refuses it for the reason this gap gives, the refusal is correct, and the ruling removes the only planned way of lifting it. The empty surface is the honest state.', "updated_at" = '2026-09-25 05:02', "updated_by_session" = 'session_2026-09-25-research-batch-20-audit-cluster-templer-fhwa' WHERE "gap_id" = 'GAP-024';
UPDATE "gaps" SET "status" = 'CLOSED-DECIDED', "description" = 'GAP-016 IS NOT CLOSED: REF-01002 FULL TEXT IS UNOBTAINABLE BY EVERY ROUTE AVAILABLE TO THIS ENVIRONMENT, MEASURED ACROSS SEVEN. Batch 17 was convened to read it and could not. Routes, all persisted as artefacts: academia.edu 403 on two different copies, researchgate 403, JSTOR 200 whose body is a bot interstitial, SafetyLit 503 then empty, OpenAlex 429 with the environment budget exhausted. THE INFORMATIVE ONE IS CROSSREF: a bibliographic title search returns five neighbouring papers and not this one, which VERIFIES rather than assumes the no-DOI fact the whole problem rests on -- Journal of Architectural and Planning Research never deposited it. Consensus returned the record and the same abstract, corroborating existence at index level, not full text. WHAT THIS MEANS FOR THE DETERMINATION, UNCHANGED AND SAID AGAIN BECAUSE IT IS THE POINT: extraction 45 stays skim/preliminary, REF-01002 stays UNVERIFIED, gate 1 stays open, C10 keeps refusing the re-determination, parameter 3 x MOB stays undetermined. WHAT WOULD ACTUALLY WORK, and none of it is a search: a library or document-delivery route (JSTOR institutional access, ILL, or a request to the corresponding author, whose consultancy publishes its papers). THAT IS A DIFFERENT KIND OF WORK FROM A RETRIEVAL LADDER and the next batch should plan it as such rather than re-running the same seven routes and recording a second null. AN OPEN METADATA QUESTION RIDES ALONG: TRID prints the fourth author Weiner, Jerome M; a search summary rendered it Welner, J. M. Neither is a retrieved authoritative index. The stored author row says Weiner and is UNCONFIRMED -- settle it with the same retrieval that settles the rest. || CORRECTED 2026-09-18: THREE CORRECTIONS. (1) SafetyLit: this row says 503; the persisted artefact is exit 35, 0 bytes, no HTTP response. A 503 did occur, on a separate unpersisted WebFetch afterwards -- empty first, then 503. (2) SEVEN ROUTES overst